mbent Susie Lee (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Susie Lee, a Democratic incumbent, seeks another term in a Las Vegas-area district that leans only slightly Democratic. Expert raters mostly call the race Likely Democratic, with two rating it Safe Democratic and two Lean Democratic. Prediction markets give Lee roughly a 93 to 95 percent chance of winning. No public general-election polls are available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals and expert judgment.\n\nLee has raised about $5.6 million to Martin O'Donnell's $4.1 million, though O'Donnell ends with more cash on hand. Republicans see the seat as a pickup opportunity and have promoted the 'no tax on tips' message, while a residency dispute has trailed O'Donnell. A favorable national environment for Democrats and Lee's incumbency advantage offset the challenger's fundraising. The race remains competitive on paper but clearly favors Lee.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9366, "margin": 9.91}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9036, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9329, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9282, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9091, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.906, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9242, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.942, "margin": 10.2}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.921, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9325, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.93, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9287, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8974, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.905, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9112, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.8961, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9316, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9282, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9294, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10